gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello All,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m reporting detection probability from my gdistsamp models in a manuscript and would like to include some measure of error for the detection estimate from getP() and I&#39;m wondering what the simplest way to do that is. </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Auriel</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></font></span></div></span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br></span>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<span><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792452128344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3pNrukr9G4MGEGfaopbA0_\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</span></font></span></blockquote></div><span><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Richard Chandler<div>Assistant Professor<br><div>Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources</div><div>University of Georgia</div><div><a href=\"tel:(706)%20542-5815\" value=\"+17065425815\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">706-542-5815</a></div></div><div><a href=\"http://chandlerlab.wordpress.com\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://chandlerlab.wordpress.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792452128344000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1l7pVBqMa_mCQl84iK-LCI\">Lab website</a></div></div></div></div></